  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_3">
   <item>
    <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout" columnstretch="0,1,1">
     <item row="0" column="2" rowspan="2">
      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_4">
       <item row="2" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagUseAll">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>If this is checked, then the leveled list will produce every form in its list, regardless of the player's level. This is mutually exclusive with the other options for level calculations.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Use All</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="0" colspan="2">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagRecalcPerCount">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>If this list is in another leveled list with a count greater than one, this checkbox determines whether each generated object is the same (unchecked), or whether this leveled list is calculated independently for each generated object (checked).</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Calculate for each item in count</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="0" colspan="2">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagCumulativeLevels">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>If this is checked, then the leveled list will use any list entry at or below the player's level. If unchecked, the leveled list will use the list entry that is closest to the player's level without exceeding it.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Calculate from all levels &lt;= player's level</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </item>
     <item row="1" column="0" colspan="2">
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox">
       <property name="whatsThis">
        <string>Control the likelihood that this leveled list won't spawn anything at all. If you select a Global, its value will be treated as a percentage (i.e. in the range [0, 100]) and used instead of the fixed percentage. Note that the Creation Kit only lets you edit the fixed percentage, though a Global should still work in-game.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="title">
        <string>Chance None</string>
       </property>
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="horizontalLayout">
        <item>
         <widget class="QSpinBox" name="chanceNonePercentage">
